ent on this frame, so there is nothing to conflict with.\n  - The three degrees are accurate for the record as built: an entry's position and hash, and a document's digest, are what two parties can cite in common.\n\nOne wording point, not blocking. \"So a room needs two kinds of act that no application defines\" reads as if pointing and claims sit outside every package. The companion design note (0e06e751, head 77d0c552) proposes them as a commons package that every room installs. \"that belong to the room, not to any one application\" would say the same thing without contradicting the note. If you take it, the change is one line and no re-review is needed.\n\nArchitecture: sound for a catalogue page. The frame separates what is fixed for all members (acts, guards, exact versions, reads, item ends) from what is each party's (meaning, cast, presentation, own closing). It adds no claim that anything is built.\n\nSimplification: acceptable. The new section replaces a flat six-item list with two short lists that say who fixes each part. The two added sentences in \"Three kinds of statement\" connect the old terms to the new ones without renaming either.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head 18103d2b. Documents only; no gate is owed. The planner lands it.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:378238cbd416d421895539b8b028363e87216c8d","binding":"assigned","head":"18103d2b311ee557c0fb368027d52762e51c53ef","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7812d01c5ec14a0954b7472f9ccff0737b59c888\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6480d146e6fac7e8039ebe375eec4a0c114c6b59\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2d1bb9a000949ca573c1ba81cdec0d5ea3a64ce0","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}